WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Even at our current peak of
technological sophistication and scale,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.850
human civilization is infinitesimally small
compared to the actual limits

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.767
of physical possibility in the universe.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:16.717
But according to our logic, automation is not
exactly a replacement for human labor,

00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:21.433
but an amplifier or a force multiplier
of human labor.

00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:25.483
Rather than space being the reward for
achieving a perfect society on Earth,

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:29.833
the only way to achieve a functional,
although certainly not a perfect society,

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:34.533
is, you know, the only way to impose the discipline
on us to achieve a functional society

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:37.833
is by pursuing space expansion,
and in particular,

00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:39.533
interstellar space expansion,

00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:42.333
rather than just interplanetary
in the solar system.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:46.767
The way to preserve humanity is not
to limit industry, but to unleash it.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:49.767
And perhaps if we have enough people
spreading throughout the universe,

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:54.917
it will truly become impossible for any one
tyrant or sclerotic system

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:56.667
to dominate all of humanity.
